<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Enver Hoxha</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1908">1908</a>–<a href="/years/1985">1985</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/20th-century">20th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Enver Hoxha was the communist ruler of Albania from 1944 until his death in 1985. A founder and first secretary of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/party-of-labour-of-albania">Albanian Communist Party</a> in 1941, he led the Partisans to victory in 1944 and built a Stalinist <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/dictatorship">dictatorship</a>. Breaking in turn with <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/yugoslavia">Yugoslavia</a>, the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/soviet-union">Soviet Union</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/china">China</a>, he left Albania deeply isolated, and in 1967 he declared it the world's first atheist state.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/enver-hoxha.jpg" alt="Enver Hoxha" width="320" height="425" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Petrit Kumi · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Enver_Hoxha_portrait_(colour_correction).jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
<section class="enc-quotes"><h2 class="enc-section-title">Across the Institute</h2><ul><li><blockquote>China and the Soviet Union were at sword’s point by 1960, splitting the world movement into two hostile camps, and anti-revisionists such as the Maoists and <b>Enver Hoxha</b>’s followers rejected the Soviet line after Khrushchev.</blockquote><a href="/ideology/communism">Communism · Spread &amp; Variants</a></li><li><blockquote>From within Marxism–Leninism, <b>Enver Hoxha</b> of Albania denounced Deng as a revisionist in 1978 and attacked Maoism itself, arguing that New Democracy halts class struggle, that the Three Worlds Theory is “counter-revolutionary”, and questioning Mao’s guerrilla methods.</blockquote><a href="/ideology/maoism">Maoism · Critiques &amp; Debates</a></li><li><blockquote>Albania's assembly abolished the monarchy and declared a People's Republic under communist leader <b>Enver Hoxha</b>.</blockquote><a href="/today-in-history/january-11">11 January in history</a></li><li><blockquote>Resistance grew, including <b>Enver Hoxha's</b> Communist Party, founded in 1941.</blockquote><a href="/state/albanian-kingdom-1939-1943">Albanian Kingdom (1939-1943)</a></li><li><blockquote><b>Enver Hoxha's</b> Partisans won the civil war and took Tirana on 17 November 1944 as German forces withdrew.</blockquote><a href="/state/albanian-kingdom-1943-1944">Albanian Kingdom (1943-1944)</a></li><li><blockquote><b>Enver Hoxha's</b> Communist-led Partisans took power as German forces withdrew in November 1944 from the Albanian Kingdom (1943-1944).</blockquote><a href="/state/peoples-socialist-republic-of-albania">People's Socialist Republic of Albania</a></li></ul></section>
<section class="enc-where enc-born"><h2 class="enc-section-title">Born and died</h2><p class="enc-born-p">Born in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/gjirokaster">Gjirokastër</a>, in what is now <a href="/countries/albania">Albania</a>. Died in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/tirana">Tirana</a>, in what is now <a href="/countries/albania">Albania</a>. <span class="enc-born-src">Places as Wikidata records them.</span></p><figure class="st-locator enc-loc"><a href="/atlas?at=40.08,20.14&amp;year=1958" aria-label="Gjirokastër on the atlas"><svg class="map map-loc" viewBox="5046 730 900 540" role="img" aria-label="Map: the birthplace of Enver Hoxha"><image href="/maps/world.svg" x="0" y="0" width="10000" height="4393"/><path class="map-dot-halo" d="M5496 1000h0"/><path class="map-dot-me" d="M5496 1000h0"/></svg></a><figcaption>The dot marks the birthplace. <a href="/atlas?at=40.08,20.14&amp;year=1958">What was here in 1958? &rarr;</a></figcaption></figure></section>
